counterexample:
When the unit is explicitly encoded in the variable name:
```rust
fn truncate_string_safe(input: &str, max_bytes: usize) -> &str {
    &input[..max_bytes]
}
```

fix:
Attach the unit of measurement to the parameter or variable name to make the unit explicit.
```rust
fn truncate_string(input: &str, max_chars: usize) -> &str {
    // Correctly count characters to avoid panics on multi-byte boundaries
    let byte_end = input.chars().take(max_chars).map(|c| c.len_utf8()).sum();
    &input[..byte_end]
}
```
